INT. SISTERS - CONTINUOUS

Enter TROFIMOV in a worn student uniform and spectacles.

LUBOV
What a marvellous garden! White masses of flowers, the blue sky....

TROFIMOV
Lubov Andreyevna!

She looks round at him.

TROFIMOV
I only want to show myself, and I’ll go away.

Kisses her hand warmly.

TROFIMOV
I was told to wait till the morning, but I didn’t have the patience.

LUBOV ANDREYEVNA looks surprised.

Crying.

VARYA
It’s Peter Trofimov.

TROFIMOV
Peter Trofimov, once the tutor of your Grisha.... Have I changed so much?

LUBOV ANDREYEVNA embraces him and cries softly.

Confused.

GAEV
That’s enough, that’s enough, Luba.

Weeps.

VARYA
But I told you, Peter, to wait till to-morrow.

LUBOV
My Grisha... my boy... Grisha... my son.

VARYA
What are we to do, little mother? It’s the will of God.

Softly, through his tears.

TROFIMOV
It’s all right, it’s all right.

Still weeping.

LUBOV
My boy’s dead; he was drowned. Why? Why, my friend?

Softly.

LUBOV
Anya’s asleep in there. I am speaking so loudly, making such a noise.... Well, Peter? What’s made you look so bad? Why have you grown so old?

TROFIMOV
In the train an old woman called me a decayed gentleman.

LUBOV
You were quite a boy then, a nice little student, and now your hair is not at all thick and you wear spectacles. Are you really still a student?

Goes to the door.

TROFIMOV
I suppose I shall always be a student.

Kisses her brother, then VARYA.

LUBOV
Well, let’s go to bed.... And you’ve grown older, Leonid.

Follows her.

PISCHIN
Yes, we’ve got to go to bed.... Oh, my gout! I’ll stay the night here. If only, Lubov Andreyevna, my dear, you could get me 240 roubles to-morrow morning--

GAEV
Still the same story.

PISCHIN
Two hundred and forty roubles... to pay the interest on the mortgage.

LUBOV
I haven’t any money, dear man.

PISCHIN
I’ll give it back... it’s a small sum....

LUBOV
Well, then, Leonid will give it to you.... Let him have it, Leonid.

GAEV
By all means; hold out your hand.

LUBOV
Why not? He wants it; he’ll give it back.

LUBOV ANDREYEVNA, TROFIMOV, PISCHIN, and FIERS go out. GAEV, VARYA, and YASHA remain.

GAEV
My sister hasn’t lost the habit of throwing money about.

To YASHA.

GAEV
Stand off, do; you smell of poultry.

Grins.

YASHA
You are just the same as ever, Leonid Andreyevitch.
